@page "/"

<PageTitle>Purview Telemetry Sample</PageTitle>

<h1>Purview Telemetry Source Generator - Sample App</h1>

<p class="lead">
	This Blazor application demonstrates distributed tracing between a frontend (Blazor SSR) and backend API service
	using the Purview Telemetry Source Generator.
</p>

<h2>Features Demonstrated</h2>

<ul>
	<li><strong>Distributed Tracing:</strong> Activities flow automatically between the Blazor frontend and API service via HTTP headers</li>
	<li><strong>HTTP Resiliency:</strong> Automatic retries with exponential backoff using Microsoft.Extensions.Http.Resilience</li>
	<li><strong>Service Discovery:</strong> Aspire-based service discovery for API communication</li>
	<li><strong>Multi-Target Telemetry:</strong> v4.0 feature - single method generates Activity + Log + Metric simultaneously</li>
</ul>

<h2>Try It Out</h2>

<p>Navigate to the <a href="/weather">Weather</a> page to see the API in action with:</p>
<ul>
	<li>Normal weather data fetching</li>
	<li>Failure scenario buttons to test validation errors and retry behavior</li>
</ul>

<h2>View Traces</h2>

<p>Run with the Aspire AppHost to see distributed traces in the Aspire dashboard:</p>
<pre><code>cd samples/SampleApp
dotnet run --project SampleApp.AppHost</code></pre>
